ngl `a ~ Add(r, b)` puts a + b on r
Add(r, y) vs n     => y ~ AddWith[n](r)
AddWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a + b
Sub(r, y) vs n     => y ~ SubWith[n](r)
SubWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a - b
Mul(r, y) vs n     => y ~ MulWith[n](r)
MulWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a * b
Div(r, y) vs n     => y ~ DivWith[n](r)
DivWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a / b
Mod(r, y) vs n     => y ~ ModWith[n](r)
ModWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a % b
Eq(r, y) vs n      => y ~ EqWith[n](r)
EqWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a == b
Lt(r, y) vs n      => y ~ LtWith[n](r)
LtWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a < b
Gt(r, y) vs n      => y ~ GtWith[n](r)
GtWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a > b